---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Log2Content from "../../components/Log2Content.astro";
import "../../styles/logs.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Beyond GraalVM and LLVM: Oreslang everywhere — engineering log #2"
  description="Engineering log 002: portable Oreslang backends for browsers, mobile, edge and embedded systems; compiler-enforced environment headers, imports and capability effects."
>
  <nav class="log-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/logs/">Logs</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">#2</span></nav>
  <header class="log-entry-header">
    <p class="kicker">Engineering log / 002</p>
    <details class="log-prompt-disclosure">
      <summary class="log-prompt-summary">
        <h1 class="log-prompt-heading">
          <span class="log-prompt-topline">
            <span class="log-prompt-word">prompt</span>
            <span class="log-prompt-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </span>
          <span class="log-prompt-glimmer" aria-hidden="true">besides graalvm and llvm what else is good for implementing/running a language? if we want the language to run on embedded systems/devices, mobile phones like ios/android, browsers, and edge envs ... every file probably needs a header whitelisting its environments, with imports checked by the compiler?</span>
          <span class="log-prompt-cue" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </h1>
      </summary>
      <div class="log-prompt-reveal">
        <p class="log-prompt-reveal-label">The original engineering question</p>
        <p class="log-prompt-full-text">Besides GraalVM and LLVM, what else is good for implementing or running a language? How do we reach embedded devices, iOS, Android, browsers and edge environments with Wasm or other recognized bytecode? Can every Oreslang file or package declare which environments it supports, more rigorously than “use client” and “use server”, and can the compiler verify that every transitive import complies?</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <div class="log-entry-meta"><span>Authored by <strong>Alex Mills</strong></span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><time datetime="2026-10-10">October 10, 2026</time></div>
    <p class="log-entry-intro">One portable language, many backends: Wasm, WASI, native AOT, Android DEX, JavaScript and small-device runtimes—with compile-time environment and capability checks that follow every import.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="log-entry-layout">
